} "Zhang Nan"] " reached the semi-finals, all others being eliminated in the group stage or the quarter-finals. All the quarter-final matches were really close and three of the four matches went to a deciding set. Only " [:a {:href "/athletes/133987"} "Marcus Ellis"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133986"} "Chris Langridge"] " from Britain won their match in straight sets. In the semi-final the British pair were then beaten easily in two sets by Fu and Zhang. In the final Fu Haifeng and Zhang Nan met Malaysia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/135086"} "Goh V Shem"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/135087"} "Tan Wee Kiong"] " and the Chinese pair won a very close and thrilling third set 23-21. The bronze medal went surprisingly to the British duo who beat the second Chinese pair " [:a {:href "/athletes/121935"} "Chai Biao"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133153"} "Hong Wei"] " in three sets."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/105879"} "Fu Haifeng"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/121936"} "Zhang Nan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135086"} "Goh Wei Shem"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/135087"} "Tan Wee Kiong"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MAS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MAS.png"}] "MAS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133987"} "Marcus Ellis"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/133986"} "Chris Langridge"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR